.TXT 15 10 171 0
Cg a63.000000,62.625000,431
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
}
{\plain {No periodic repetitions are falling
 in the basic summing interval [0,L-1] and
 so the value is correct. At this point,
 n = N-1, we have computed all N values 
of the DFT, which has period N. At n = N,
 we must again compute the value at n = 
0. Visualizing the period of x just off 
the plot to the left, increasing n from 
N-1 to N moves x}{\fs16 \dn6 pod(n-m,N)}{
 one step to the right, recreating the plot
 shown above for n = 0.}}
}
.TXT 12 0 41 0
Cg a45.375000,63.125000,173
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
}
{\plain {W}{e have thus shown that the correct
 values are computed for\par \par       
                       }{\ulnone   }{\ulnone 
\b  }{\ulnone \b max\{0, M+L-N-1\} <= n 
<= N-1}{\ulnone  }{\ulnone  .}}
}
