{\plain {\b \ulnone \f0 Problem 5.1}{\f0 
  Show that, if M+L-2 < N-1, then the values
 of the convolution for\par             
                     }{\b \f0   M+L-2 <=
 n <= N-1}{\f0 \par are apriori known to
 be zero. }{\f0 \f0 Modify the above example
 with an appropriate choice of L,M and N
 and carefully repeat the graphical analysis.}{\f0 
\par }{\b \f0 Hint}{\f0   The index of the
 left-most nonzero value of x}{\fs16 \dn6 
\f0 n-m}{\f0  is -(M-1)+n. If, for some 
n < N-1 this index exceeds L-1, then there
 are no nonzero products and the convolution
 sum is zero.}}
}
