{\plain {\b Exercise 5.4}{  Show that, with
 the assumed ordering 0<L<=M<=N, the left
 member of the relations (5.2) is less than
 or equal to the right member.}}
}
.TXT 5 0 44 0
Cg a64.250000,63.875000,960
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
}
{\plain {There are three cases of special
 interest to us. Note that the aperiodic
 convolution is of length M+L-1.\par \par 
    }{\b   I}{   }{\b \ulnone M = L, N =
 M+D, 0<=D<=M-1}{.  Then }{correct }{and
 not apriori known zero values          
      are computed for\par              
                                }{\b  M-D-1
 <= n <= M+D-1 = N-1}{    .             
            (5.3)\par   \par     }{\b  II}{\b 
 }{ }{\ulnone  }{\b \ulnone N=M}{.  Then
 correct }{and not apriori-known zero values
 are computed for \par \par             
     }{                          }{\ulnone 
      }{\b \ulnone L-1  <= n <=  N-1}{\ulnone 
 }{\ulnone    .}{\ulnone                
                       (5.4)\par \par   
  }{\b \ulnone III}{\ulnone  }{\ulnone  
}{\b \ulnone N=M+L-1}{\ulnone . }{\ulnone 
Then correct }{\ulnone and not apriori-known
 zero values are computed for \par \par 
                 }{\ulnone              
                  }{\b \ulnone     }{\b 
\ulnone  }{\b \ulnone 0 <= n <=  N-1}{\ulnone 
    .}{\ulnone \ulnone                  
                     (5.5)}}
}
