{\plain {\b \fs24 Convolution Computation
 over a Restricted Range}}
}
.TXT 3 10 46 0
Cg a64.000000,63.625000,683
{\rtf1\ansi \deff0
{\fonttbl
{\f0\fnil Arial;}
}
{\plain {It may happen that the aperiodic
 convolution is required only over a restricted
 range. In a signal design problem discussed
 below, the filter output is known to be
 of interest only over a small range of 
indices. Also, when estimating a covariance
 sequence (}{\ul \b Sec. 25}{), its principal
 support is typically over a restricted 
range of indices. We assume that the two
 sequences to be convolved are of equal 
length: M = L. We take N = M + D  where 
D an integer in [0,M-1]. We have already
 seen, in case (i) mentioned above, that
 the periodic convolution will be correct
 for n in [M-D-1,M+D-1]. It happens that
 this is the interval of most interest in
 filtering problems.}}
}
.ATT
.STATUS Go to Section 25, p. 4
.GOTO 25_bk.mcd
.ATT_END
